// Every branch condition (== != > < >= <=) against positive, zero and
// negative values, and the test types: a narrow signed type tests its low
// bits as a signed value, a float type tests the value. Each case shifts
// $r29 left and adds 1 if the branch was taken, so $r29 ends up holding
// the outcomes, the first case in the most significant bit.

    || + $r29 ($i64) $r29 $r29 ;              // shift the outcomes left
    || ? ($i64) $r1 == $goto t0 ;                // expect not taken
    || ? ($i64) $r0 == $goto n0 ;            // not taken: skip the +1
